00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
hi there steve kaufman  here and today i want to talk about  learning three languages  in the same day because i've changed my  strategy and i'm going to explain why  and i'm going to provide some background  some people will say gee steve you used  to say you should focus entirely on one  language and i did use to say that but a  number of things have changed  i have come to realize that  you know the more you focus on one thing  to try to nail one thing you stay with  one thing there is a point when the  efficiency the learning efficiency  declines  i find that uh  you know listening to arabic or  persian  stories that by about the second or  third story  that i'm reading or listening to i am  less focused less curious less hungry i  notice fewer things  that's one thing now i had mentioned  before that i was going to study three  languages over the next say year or so  three months on arabic three months on  persian and three months on turkish and  that was my intention  then i saw a video where a polyglot that  i greatly admire luca lampariello  who said he was doing three languages a  day  can't remember which ones i think danish  was in there  and he was spending 30 minutes on each  so i thought well if luke is doing that  maybe it's something that i should try  and so i've started doing it and the  advantage is  first of all that you are introducing  more variety so before you get stale in  one language you move on to another and  so it's new and it's it's fresh and  you're more curious  uh and i do find that since i started  doing this two days ago  i do notice things more especially when  listening but also even when reading  and uh now i am working on the mini  story so it's it's largely a matter of  refreshing where i was because i was  away for a month traveling and i dabbled  a bit in cerebral croatian and and of  course the last language i did was  turkish and so now my arabic is a little  bit rusty so  um the first thing of course is that i  find that i notice things better the  second thing is that there's less time  to forget things so it is a bit annoying  if i meet an arab arabic speaker as i  did in spain and i have to present  excuses that well yeah i was studying  arabic but for the last six months i was  doing persian and turkish and now i  can't remember my arabic and so this way  i can maintain them all every day  because i do  say two or three as i said i'm focusing  right now on reviewing my mini stories i  want to do two three four mini stories  in each language every day and i do the  same ones in each language which has the  advantage that i'm you know aware of the  context of the story because i just  finished doing it in another language  and that sort of helps  so i'm going to do that  and we'll see how it goes now people say  well you're contradicting yourself yes  i'm contradicting myself  but  the number one rule in language learning  is to enjoy it  and so  experimenting with different ways of  learning is a way of enjoying it you've  got to have fun now  obviously this learning strategy is  going to depend on your situation when i  was learning chinese  i worked for the canadian government  i had a job to learn chinese so i was  totally focused on learning mandarin  chinese  and yet even there i did have variety  because i had three hours a day of one  on one classroom instruction with a lot  of drills i had to spend a fair amount  of time every day on characters and on  writing so and then i did a lot of  listening and i also scoured the  bookstores of hong kong to find new  material to listen to and read so there  was within my mandarin learning activity  i tried to introduce as much  variety as possible  so that's one situation but now i'm  learning for fun so those of us who are  learning for fun we can experiment with  whatever system we want the main  objective is to enjoy it if you enjoy  the activity you will improve i'm quite  convinced of that  and the other you know the advantage to  me is that if i can do three a day three  languages a day say half an hour on each  particularly varying the listening  activity and if that enables me to  progress now bear in mind probably the  first month i'll be focused on the mini  stories kind of to get back to where i  was and make sure that that's you know  firmer in my mind then as i go to you  know explore new material i won't have  the advantage of being able to do the  same story in different languages so  we'll see how that all works but if it  is successful it means that  at the end of nine months rather than  being six months removed from my arabic  in fact i will have all the three  languages with me learning them all  together and i and i think that that you  know we should experiment with language  learning because unfortunately language  learning and language instruction for  too long  has been the preserve of the language  teachers so the assumption is that you  learn in a classroom  what you may learn in a classroom  but it's also just as likely that you  what you do outside the classroom is  more important than what you do in the  classroom the reason why people in  sweden and holland  or croatia  speak english well is because they have  so many movies and television programs  in english or in the original language  for other languages so it's not because  necessarily language instruction in  croatia or sweden is superior to  language instruction say in spain  i also once saw a study put out by the  american  center for linguistics or something  which traced  you know the influence of  english instructional instructional  hours  on how well immigrants did in learning  english and the  while they  sort of crowed about the benefits if you  looked at the results you sh it showed  that in some cases increased  instructional hours meant a decline in  english proficiency which really only  demonstrated that there was no direct  relationship there was all kinds of  difficulty measuring how well people are  doing  uh  and in fact  those immigrants who had friends  in you know the united states this was  an american study or who worked where  they used english obviously we're going  to improve more than people who only  went to class and so that really the  instructional the idea of focusing all  language learning on the classroom and  therefore language learning  uh methodology or the best way to  proceed has to be based on what works in  a classroom i think that's basically  wrong i think serious language learners  should experiment with different ways of  learning  and um  you know this whole idea of learning  more than one language of being a  polyglot is something that i wasn't even  aware of when i was studying chinese i  just had this one task  but i you know i didn't even know the  meaning of the word polyglot basically  because linguist was is the word still  in english that's used to describe  someone who speaks many languages  but as i learned more and more languages  i realized the benefit of varying it not  only varying the activities  but also varying the the language and i  find that it makes me more focused  better um you know more attentive to the  language  and of course the brain likes novelty  so i'm going to continue experimenting  with this  and we'll tell you you know we'll let  you know how it goes a small note here  um back of course for my trip to  croatian spain  but on the 15th i'm going to japan i'm  going to attend the polyglot conference  in fukuoka and i'm going to be in japan  from the 16th to the 23rd  seven days  uh  if anybody wants to have a meet-up i'll  be in fukuoka and osaka possibly tokyo  please let me know if there's any desire  for a meet up  i will make a presentation at the  fukuoka polyglot conference and also i  will leave a link here to  a presentation that i'm going to make  to a group of japanese language learners  this one will be in japanese  and you'll see the link and if anyone is  in fukuoka  also welcome to join it  [Music]  all right that was just again inviting  people to let me know if they won't have  a meet up so that's it and i will  continue doing my three languages a day  because i'm having fun with it all right  then bye for now  [Music]  you

